Emacsvox News -- Unreleased User-Visible Changes

Maintained by Emacsvox Contributors.

* Emacsvox Unreleased --- Current User-Visible Changes

This file records user-visible changes made after Emacsvox 2026.9.0.  Add new
entries here during development without choosing the next release series in
advance.  Before a release, replace =Unreleased= with the exact value from
=VERSION= and complete the release notes.

Released notes are preserved in [[file:NEWS-2026.9.0][NEWS for Emacsvox 2026.9.0]].

- Opt-in Aural Presentation diagnostics now correlate native submission IDs
  with Omnivox dispatch IDs and record actual dispatch send, first observed
  mixer-source consumption, and terminal playback timing.  Omnivox's normal
  session log supplies the matching server admission, queue, synthesis, and
  playback-stage breakdown without a speech protocol change.  Use =C-e d D=
  to toggle the sensitive, full-text diagnostic log for the current session.

- The source-built Windows Omnivox runtime now includes the checksum-locked
  RuTTS 6.3.3 companion and its built-in male and female Russian voices.  RuLex
  remains excluded.
